================================================================================================
(iv) linear vs quadratic.  At q=1/2 the reflection symmetry lm(n)=lm(T-n) kills the
     odd orders in lambda (paper 3's cosh pairing).  At q != 1/2 complementation maps
     q to 1-q, NOT q to q, so the symmetry is broken and a LINEAR term should survive.
     Structural prediction: the first-order coefficient is
        L^{(q)} = SUM_d delta_d [ q^{N_d} - (1-q)^{N_d} ],   identically 0 at q=1/2.
